{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Sc5hEtCg826F9AYH4CXjfk","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd077-cksum\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/cksum: Print CRC Checksum and Byte Count\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  macOS ships a BSD cksum that differs from GNU cksum in algorithm selection and output\n6\t  format options. GNU cksum supports CRC-32 (POSIX default), as well as modern hash\n7\t  algorithms via --algorithm. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference\n8\t  binary (gcksum, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on all flag combinations,\n9\t  verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n10\t\n11\tgoals:\n12\t  - G1: Compute CRC-32 checksums and byte counts for files or stdin in POSIX format.\n13\t  - G2: Support --algorithm flag for alternate digest algorithms (sm3, blake2b, sha1, sha224, sha256, sha384, sha512).\n14\t  - G3: Support --untagged and --raw output format control.\n15\t  - G4: Verify functional parity against gcksum via differential testing.\n16\t\n17\trequirements:\n18\t  R1:\n19\t    title: Default CRC checksum\n20\t    items:\n21\t      - R1.1:\n22\t          text: Must compute the POSIX CRC-32 checksum of each named file and print one line per file in the format \"CHECKSUM BYTES FILENAME\".\n23\t      - R1.2:\n24\t          text: Must read from stdin when no file arguments are given. Stdin output omits the filename.\n25\t      - R1.3:\n26\t          text: Must process multiple files in argument order, printing one line per file.\n27\t      - R1.4:\n28\t          text: Must exit 1 when any named file cannot be opened, printing an error to stderr, and continue processing remaining files.\n29\t\n30\t  R2:\n31\t    title: Algorithm selection and output format\n32\t    items:\n33\t      - R2.1:\n34\t          text: \"--algorithm=ALG selects the digest algorithm. Supported values: crc (default), sm3, blake2b, sha1, sha224, sha256, sha384, sha512. Non-CRC algorithms produce tagged output by default (e.g., 'SHA256 (file) = HASH').\"\n35\t      - R2.2:\n36\t          text: \"--untagged produces traditional GNU hash output ('HASH  FILENAME') instead of tagged BSD format when used with non-CRC algorithms.\"\n37\t      - R2.3:\n38\t          text: \"--raw outputs the raw binary digest instead of hex-encoded text. Only valid with non-CRC algorithms.\"\n39\t\n40\t  R3:\n41\t    title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n42\t    items:\n43\t      - R3.1:\n44\t          text: Must exit 0 when all files are processed successfully.\n45\t      - R3.2:\n46\t          text: Must exit 1 when any file cannot be opened or an invalid algorithm is specified.\n47\t      - R3.3:\n48\t          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n49\t\n50\tnon_goals:\n51\t  - cmd/cksum does not implement --check mode for CRC verification (GNU cksum supports --check only for non-CRC algorithms).\n52\t  - cmd/cksum does not implement --base64 encoding.\n53\t\n54\tacceptance_criteria:\n55\t  - id: AC1\n56\t    criterion: \"cksum on a known file produces the correct CRC checksum and byte count, matching gcksum.\"\n57\t    traces:\n58\t      - R1.1\n59\t      - R1.2\n60\t      - R1.3\n61\t      - R1.4\n62\t  - id: AC2\n63\t    criterion: \"cksum --algorithm=sha256 on a file produces tagged SHA-256 output, matching gcksum --algorithm=sha256.\"\n64\t    traces:\n65\t      - R2.1\n66\t      - R2.2\n67\t  - id: AC3\n68\t    criterion: \"Differential test against gcksum passes for all required test cases.\"\n69\t    traces:\n70\t      - R1.1\n71\t      - R1.2\n72\t      - R1.3\n73\t      - R1.4\n74\t      - R2.1\n75\t  - id: AC4\n76\t    criterion: \"cmd/cksum compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n77\t    traces:\n78\t      - R1.1\n79\t      - R1.2\n80\t      - R1.3\n81\t      - R1.4\n82\t      - R2.1\n83\t      - R2.2\n84\t      - R2.3\n85\t      - R3.1\n86\t      - R3.2\n87\t      - R3.3\n88\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6aff05fe-27d9-4cf9-95e0-d6b033e43629","uuid":"0847016a-6a1b-4a7f-afd5-d7fdc8ef1c04","timestamp":"2026-05-23T02:20:25.982Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5503/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd077-cksum.yaml","content":"id: srd077-cksum\ntitle: \"cmd/cksum: Print CRC Checksum and Byte Count\"\n\nproblem: |\n  macOS ships a BSD cksum that differs from GNU cksum in algorithm selection and output\n  format options. GNU cksum supports CRC-32 (POSIX default), as well as modern hash\n  algorithms via --algorithm. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference\n  binary (gcksum, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on all flag combinations,\n  verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Compute CRC-32 checksums and byte counts for files or stdin in POSIX format.\n  - G2: Support --algorithm flag for alternate digest algorithms (sm3, blake2b, sha1, sha224, sha256, sha384, sha512).\n  - G3: Support --untagged and --raw output format control.\n  - G4: Verify functional parity against gcksum via differential testing.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Default CRC checksum\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: Must compute the POSIX CRC-32 checksum of each named file and print one line per file in the format \"CHECKSUM BYTES FILENAME\".\n      - R1.2:\n          text: Must read from stdin when no file arguments are given. Stdin output omits the filename.\n      - R1.3:\n          text: Must process multiple files in argument order, printing one line per file.\n      - R1.4:\n          text: Must exit 1 when any named file cannot be opened, printing an error to stderr, and continue processing remaining files.\n\n  R2:\n    title: Algorithm selection and output format\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: \"--algorithm=ALG selects the digest algorithm. Supported values: crc (default), sm3, blake2b, sha1, sha224, sha256, sha384, sha512. Non-CRC algorithms produce tagged output by default (e.g., 'SHA256 (file) = HASH').\"\n      - R2.2:\n          text: \"--untagged produces traditional GNU hash output ('HASH  FILENAME') instead of tagged BSD format when used with non-CRC algorithms.\"\n      - R2.3:\n          text: \"--raw outputs the raw binary digest instead of hex-encoded text. Only valid with non-CRC algorithms.\"\n\n  R3:\n    title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n    items:\n      - R3.1:\n          text: Must exit 0 when all files are processed successfully.\n      - R3.2:\n          text: Must exit 1 when any file cannot be opened or an invalid algorithm is specified.\n      - R3.3:\n          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/cksum does not implement --check mode for CRC verification (GNU cksum supports --check only for non-CRC algorithms).\n  - cmd/cksum does not implement --base64 encoding.\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"cksum on a known file produces the correct CRC checksum and byte count, matching gcksum.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"cksum --algorithm=sha256 on a file produces tagged SHA-256 output, matching gcksum --algorithm=sha256.\"\n    traces:\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"Differential test against gcksum passes for all required test cases.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R2.1\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"cmd/cksum compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R3.3\n","numLines":88,"startLine":1,"totalLines":88}}}
